WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.757
It all started one Monday morning at school.

2
00:00:17.758 --> 00:00:22.868
"It" was my idea—my first invention!

3
00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:26.889
We were sitting in class, coloring maps.

4
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:32.188
I don't understand why our teacher, Mrs. Romano, makes us color maps.

5
00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.800
She acts as if we are in first grade instead of fourth grade.

6
00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:42.196
Does she really think we still like to color?

7
00:00:42.197 --> 00:00:44.159
"Use bright colors!"

8
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.316
Mrs. Romano said, walking around the room.

9
00:00:49.317 --> 00:00:52.656
I colored North America green.

10
00:00:52.657 --> 00:00:57.360
I colored South America orange.

11
00:00:57.361 --> 00:01:00.591
I colored Africa yellow.

12
00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:06.417
Then I started working on Asia, which is a really big continent.

13
00:01:06.418 --> 00:01:08.979
My hand was getting tired.

14
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:12.559
I stopped to give it a rest.

15
00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.978
My friend Molly leaned toward me.

16
00:01:14.979 --> 00:01:18.081
"Psst, Iggy!" she whispered.

17
00:01:18.082 --> 00:01:20.524
"My hand hurts from coloring!"

18
00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:23.874
"So does mine!" I said.

19
00:01:23.875 --> 00:01:29.250
"Quiet, please!" said Mrs. Romano.

20
00:01:29.251 --> 00:01:34.564
"All I want to hear is the sound of crayons moving across the paper."

21
00:01:34.565 --> 00:01:39.751
Mrs. Romano wanted to hear the sound of crayons moving across the paper?

22
00:01:39.752 --> 00:01:43.013
I was so tired of that sound!

23
00:01:43.014 --> 00:01:46.010
"Why aren't there machines to do coloring?"

24
00:01:46.011 --> 00:01:48.711
I thought suddenly.

25
00:01:48.712 --> 00:01:54.271
"Then kids wouldn't have to work so hard."

26
00:01:54.272 --> 00:02:00.368
That was when I got my idea—a truly incredible idea.

27
00:02:00.369 --> 00:02:07.692
It could make me, Iggy, a famous inventor!

28
00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:12.802
I told Molly about my idea on the way home from school.

29
00:02:12.803 --> 00:02:15.369
"Wow!" said Molly.

30
00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:21.162
"If your idea works, we'll never have to color by hand again!"

31
00:02:21.163 --> 00:02:25.620
Our school is near the apartment building where Molly and I live.

32
00:02:25.621 --> 00:02:30.808
Our apartments are both on the fifth floor.

33
00:02:30.809 --> 00:02:37.952
That means we have to climb a lot of stairs every day.

34
00:02:37.953 --> 00:02:44.872
"Whew, I wish our backpacks weren't so heavy!" I groaned.

35
00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:56.486
"Me too," she agreed, panting hard.

36
00:02:56.487 --> 00:03:02.154
I said good-bye to Molly and then went into my apartment.

37
00:03:02.155 --> 00:03:06.178
My mom was on the telephone in the kitchen.

38
00:03:06.179 --> 00:03:10.178
She waved to me as I walked by.

39
00:03:10.179 --> 00:03:15.136
I went into my bedroom and dumped my heavy backpack on the floor.

40
00:03:15.137 --> 00:03:19.800
One of its straps fell just over the chalk line on the floor.

41
00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:26.165
My older brother, Tate, had drawn the line to divide our room into two sections.

42
00:03:26.166 --> 00:03:29.964
"Hey, get your backpack off my side of the room!"

43
00:03:29.965 --> 00:03:32.051
Tate ordered me.

44
00:03:32.052 --> 00:03:36.289
"It's my room too!" I shot back.

45
00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:41.343
"No arguing, boys!" called my mother from the kitchen.

46
00:03:41.344 --> 00:03:46.478
I decided to go down to the fourth floor and see my friend Josh.

47
00:03:46.479 --> 00:03:49.896
I wanted to get away from Tate.

48
00:03:49.897 --> 00:03:54.399
Plus, I needed help with my invention.

49
00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:59.038
I knocked on the door of his apartment, and Josh answered right away.

50
00:03:59.039 --> 00:04:01.749
"Hi, Josh!" I said.

51
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.554
Josh invited me in.

52
00:04:04.555 --> 00:04:09.433
"Do you know that toy that Sparky likes?" I blurted out.

53
00:04:09.434 --> 00:04:13.883
Sparky is Josh's pet hamster.

54
00:04:13.884 --> 00:04:17.634
"His seesaw?" Josh asked.

55
00:04:17.635 --> 00:04:22.169
He walked over to Sparky's cage and lifted up the toy.

56
00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.152
"Yes, that's it," I said.

57
00:04:25.153 --> 00:04:26.350
"Can I borrow it?

58
00:04:26.351 --> 00:04:30.231
I want to make one just like it."

59
00:04:30.232 --> 00:04:32.995
"Why?" asked Josh.

60
00:04:32.996 --> 00:04:36.726
"I have a brilliant idea!" I said.

61
00:04:36.727 --> 00:04:40.310
"I'm going to invent an automatic coloring machine!

62
00:04:40.311 --> 00:04:46.006
My hand will never get tired from coloring again."

63
00:04:46.007 --> 00:04:48.690
Josh's eyes lit up.

64
00:04:48.691 --> 00:04:53.521
"Cool," he said. "How will it work?"

65
00:04:53.522 --> 00:04:56.409
"You'll see!" I told him.

66
00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:01.268
"Let's show Sparky's seesaw to Mr. Calabria, the building superintendent.

67
00:05:01.269 --> 00:05:06.087
He has a lot of wood downstairs."

68
00:05:06.088 --> 00:05:10.580
We went down the steps to the building's basement.

69
00:05:10.581 --> 00:05:17.629
Mr. Calabria was in his workroom surrounded by tools and wood scraps.

70
00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.390
He smiled at us.

71
00:05:19.391 --> 00:05:24.416
"Is your kitchen faucet leaking again, Iggy?" he asked.

72
00:05:24.417 --> 00:05:25.972
I shook my head.

73
00:05:25.973 --> 00:05:29.139
"Our faucet is working fine."

74
00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.718
"Then do you have another problem?" he asked.

75
00:05:32.719 --> 00:05:36.918
"He has something, Mr. Calabria!" Josh burst out.

76
00:05:36.919 --> 00:05:45.798
"But it's not a problem—it's an amazing, incredible idea!"
